    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15056" root="رحل" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَحِيلٌ</span></b>  A camel <i>having the saddle</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَحْل</span> [not
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رحالة</span> as in Freytag's Lex.]) <i>put upon him;</i> as
also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْحُولٌ</span></b> . (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُحْلَةٌ</span>, in four
places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  As a simple subst, or, accord. to the
Msb, an inf. n.: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِحْلَةٌ</span>.

